# Prune the full 2026-03-09 Wikidata network down to a size an ordinary
# machine can hold, and write the result under a NEW name.
#
#   build-release/bin/zelph < dev_scripts/prune-full-dump.zph
#
# This is a deliberate, exclusive operation: the source is 88 GB on disk and
# roughly 210 GB resident, so it needs ZRAM, swap and the priority script, and
# it drives the machine to its limits for as long as it runs. Do not start it
# beside anything else that matters.
#
# The output name is NOT the one the shipped artifact carries.
# `wikidata-20260309-all-pruned.bin` is mirrored to Hugging Face and is what
# `mkdocs/docs/class-hierarchy.md` was re-verified against on 7 August 2026 --
# 78 topmost culprits of 18 933 affected classes, and a closure index of
# 1 193 228 edges. `wikidata-prune.zph` was rewritten from measurement since
# then (commit 8a5a332) and now reaches about 46 % of the file's entities, so
# the new file is a different artifact. Overwriting the old one would retire
# every documented number without a trace; compare the two instead.
#
# `.quit` and not `.exit`: the latter is not a command, so it reports an
# unknown command and leaves the session running.

.load /home/stefan/zelph/wikidata-20260309-all.bin
.import examples/wikidata/wikidata-prune
.save /home/stefan/zelph/wikidata-20260309-all-pruned-v2.bin
.quit
